<b>יד.</b> "And he shall slaughter it" - see Beit Yaakov siman 108. Taz writes that saying "u-neshalmah parim sefateinu" before the tamid and Eizehu Mekoman is an error, since chatat is mentioned there and one may not be liable, akin to bringing unconsecrated offerings in the courtyard. Rather say it specifically in place of the tamid offering.
